<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  An A320 for JSBSim, fitted to the project's acceptance targets. GPLv3, like everything in flight/.

  Written for this project; not derived from JSBSim's own A320 or 737 files. The engines are JSBSim's
  CFM56_5 (25,000 lb, the A320-211's CFM56-5A1), read at run time from the pinned clone as the 737 reads
  its CFM56. The surfaces are positioned by the A32NX servos through flight/jsbsim/a32nx-surfaces.xml,
  which JSBSim loads after this file.

  Where the numbers come from:
    geometry          A32NX's MSFS flight model (fbw-a32nx/.../FlyByWire_A320_NEO/flight_model.cfg,
                      GPLv3): wing area and span with sharklets, tail areas; MAC 4.1935 m from OpenAP's
                      a320.yml (LGPL-3.0)
    weight, inertia   the same file's weight and balance, an airline's A320-251N: operating empty weight
                      42.5 t at 30 % MAC, empty moments of inertia. MSFS names its axes differently: its
                      pitch, roll and yaw moments are JSBSim's iyy, ixx and izz
    loading           ours: 65.0 t, CG 28 % MAC; payload 14.5 t, fuel 8.0 t in A32NX's tank layout
    aerodynamics      the coefficients below, each a property under aero/fit/. A seed is what a value
                      started from before the fit and where the seed came from; see
                      flight/jsbsim/aircraft/A320-fit/seeds.csv. The fitter (flight/harness/fit.cpp)
                      rewrites the values here and nothing else
    ground effect     ours, from textbook theory: lift by the effective aspect ratio of a wing over its
                      image (DATCOM's lift-curve slope), induced drag by McCormick's factor
                      (16 h/b)^2 / (1 + (16 h/b)^2)

  Frames. Structure: x aft from the nose, y right, z up, inches. Surfaces as JSBSim reads them:
  elevator, stabiliser and aileron positive trailing edge down, the aileron as the left aileron's share
  of the differential; rudder positive trailing edge left. Spoilers as the share of full extension on
  each wing, all five panels at 50 deg being 1.

  Built from public data and estimates, for education and entertainment; not endorsed by Airbus, not
  to be sold. This project sells nothing.
-->
<fdm_config name="A320-fit" version="2.0" release="ALPHA"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="http://jsbsim.sourceforge.net/JSBSim.xsd">

